msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:29
#: 9feb96652540461bb9f3fa2f0a7abda6
msgid "Assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:31
#: 5efc22e7a97d463c9a8377da9043f6ba
msgid "**Solder the right angle 9x3 pin connector that was included with your PX4FMU kit to the side of the PX4IO board that has \"PX4 autopilot\" printed on it.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:35
#: 294beba383ee4f8481fa9457ed16537f
msgid "When you insert the 9 x 3 connector into the PX4IO board put it in with the plastic spacer on the connector facing to the back of the board, NOT down against the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:39
#: a10d60b17031496d939bca1ec93780be
msgid "Solder the small white PAP-02-VS 2 pin connector into the 2 holes directly behind the battery pads on the PX4IO board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:41
#: 29b2455248f64f3f9abe5ff60adddc96
msgid "**Install the PX4IO board on top of the PX4FMU board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:43
#: dbdfe52bfe8f4c0a8a61d10e38c080a9
msgid "To protect the barometer from wind, gusts, motion effects and prop wash:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:46
#: 3744dbb6179549b5834c1ee3b371e8f9
msgid "Cut a piece of 1/2\" thick soft foam to the size of the PX4FMU board minus the inter-board connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:48
#: c2e19482c5b9455fb42d02563132bbf8
msgid "Place place the piece of 1/2\" foam between the PX4FMU board and the PX4IO board before you connect them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:50
#: 78ce530f96334fb8b910ab9fa9bf4249
msgid "An enclosure could mitigate barometer problems too, but ensure that it does not interfere with the compass (magnetometer)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:53
#: 188d58a02bc74c7da9e6c7b036a281c3
msgid "Connect the PX4FMU board to the PX4IO board and ensure all of the connector pins are straight and insertion is complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:55
#: 288d817db36f4b07ab7f1a0d674925bf
msgid "Mount the PX4-FMU + PX4-IO board stack in a central and level location on top of your Copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:57
#: 1d5c53749b664fcaa8f3c2181d0adc09
msgid "The PX4FMU board is normally on top."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:58
#: e75c9454769549009b5f4a7b2fd0f436
msgid "It can be advantageous to mount the PX4IO board on top to provide for better Connector access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:60
#: cadfb5a93f4b44708dedd42ed4b856c4
msgid "If you do mount the PX4IO board on top it will be necessary to set the \"Board Orientation (AHRS_ORIENTATION)\" parameter to **8** i.e \"Roll 180\", in the Advanced Parameter List in Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:63
#: 106dbfb45d7f4cd1b728304de89ddcf9
msgid "The arrow labeled \"FRONT\" should be facing to the front of the aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:65
#: eec29e881ddb4277bf78023b46227309
msgid "The Micro SD memory card holder should face to the back of the Aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:68
#: f09171d8fb87490b83006e2daf3a1213
msgid "**Use the included standoffs and hardware.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:70
#: 084170a07c204376a2ebe4692bcbf66c
msgid "Which ever side of which ever board is going to be on top but a black standoff through one of the mounting holes from the bottom and thread a black plastic nut onto it from the top."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:73
#: 1753925861b941eda37ef2498be135fc
msgid "Repeat the above for the remaining 3 holes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:74
#: 66d21be820354a88a6aedbc363ed1f00
msgid "Connect the PX4FMU and PX4IO board insuring no pins are bent on the board interconnection connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:76
#: 0f3d6eefd4e3479399ceca510aba5a3e
msgid "Thread 4 more of the black standoffs into the already installed black standoffs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:79
#: a425ea93ebb443e6a1a4b13d1afa627b
msgid "**In order to reduce DC EMF effect on the compass see** :ref:`Magnetic Interference <common-magnetic-interference>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:80
#: 94a983027ed44792a006384eb28f04ef
msgid "You will need additional vibration damping and should review :ref:`Vibration Damping <common-vibration-damping>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:83
#: cf33b2f0ac71434a967147dd4f5ef82b
msgid "At a minimum you should mount the standoffs to an intermediate plate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:85
#: aaabcc2709c4477b91324925280d5bfb
msgid "Mount the plate to your airframe with 4 small (<1\")square pads of Kyosho \"Zeal\" gel or \"Moon Gel\" in the corners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:88
#: ca852cf99b37476ea3c2fb1de43e2590
msgid "**Mount the GPS facing up with an unobstructed \"view\" of the sky.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:90
#: 258707a98fb44154a7d26866a55470af
msgid "Connect the GPS cable to the GPS connector on the PX4FMU board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:91
#: 7dc91ade3b5e4ef792dfe4addbc15400
msgid "The GPS must be positioned so that its cable will connect without strain to the PX4FMU's GPS connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:93
#: eebf1eee359e408fa4cc33cfdfa4f752
msgid "The GPS can be mounted on a short riser to give it the widest satellite access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:97
#: 3a87f110304449309a804ab6663d13ca
msgid "Wire the PX4FMU and PX4IO boards to Your Copter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:99
#: b214c278854f4284b446f755eb0e4561
msgid "**Wire the PX4-IO board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:101
#: b355625bc1d2448490b380e9dd27e3f4
msgid "The PX4IO board has a built in Power Supply which can connect to up to 18 volts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:103
#: 8eb4eebefe6e4e4b8dfa3c5a0e00275a
msgid "Insert the white PAP-02-VS 2 pin connector with the black and red wires coming out of it into the mating power connector you soldered in previously on the PX4IO board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:106
#: 564c4ec11ce746b5a6bbfdf997c0716e
msgid "Battery Plus is the(red wire) and should be soldered to your battery red power lead / connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:108
#: 773ccfcc415b475b9cd9178688894de4
msgid "Battery Ground is the(black wire) and should be soldered to your battery black battery (Ground) lead / connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:110
#: ec2dcc23e1ec4180a4dfd56fc673d9bf
msgid "The main power inputs of your ESC's will also need to connect to these wires and to a battery connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:112
#: 06659516458748948a42c8c97b22bd37
msgid "A Power Distribution board can also be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:114
#: 48fb2a69671b48b0ac83dbae789fe2da
msgid "**Connect your PPM-Sum RC receiver's 3 wire cable to the end of the 9 x 3 angle connector that is nearest the edge of the PX4IO board with the signal wire furthest from the board and the ground closest to the board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:118
#: 7275475a77a54d6db4d72482e359bf13
msgid "**Wire the PX4FMU board's servo out signals to your ESC control inputs.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:120
#: 07427b6934394d70807035cfebc99da5
msgid "Run the Signal wires ONLY from the ESCs to the 3 x 9 Servo Connector on the PX4IO board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:122
#: e659becdcb5345a8bdfd6a9eacc89709
msgid "The PX4IO board connector for Motor 1 is at the edge of the connector next to the Battery power in wires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:124
#: c6a3c3627da445da955ae0b227e892b2
msgid "Insert the Motor ESC wires arranged progressively from that edge, (1,2,3,4,etc) for 4 to 8 motors depending on your copter type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:126
#: 66493c05313541fb9079e25c09ddeb96
msgid "You can put the ESC Signal wires into a single inline connector with the correct number of pins for your copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:128
#: b1f7cd02d57842af9c7dd11b09244f47
msgid "The ESC Signal Wires / connector should be plugged into the top row (furthest from the board) of the PX4IO boards 3 x 9 Servo Connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:132
#: e3a4437a10ec4fab8493966480945797
msgid "**Note, the cable that is supplied in the plastic envelope with the UBLOX GPS which has white 6 pin connectors on both ends is not the correct cable for the PX4FMU board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:136
#: afed93bcabab4f0eb9eae46c7704660c
msgid "The correct longer cable is provided in a separate envelope and has a 5 pin \"beige\" connector on one end and a 6 pin white connector on the other end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:139
#: d6f6cad1d67c43e49a71d6df6beabc48
msgid "Plug the correct GPS cable's white 6 pin connector into the 6 pin socket on the GPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:141
#: ccf87b35e7df4d1aaa8ac8b45837f6e5
msgid "Plug the beige 5 pin connector into the PX4FMU board's 5 pin GPS socket which is next to the 15 pin DF13 Mini connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:144
#: 70f0c373e3794860aacc665e8d31bb09
msgid "**Plug the 2 pin connector attached to the lead supplied with the buzzer into the buzzer socket on the side of the PX4FMU board that has the SD card holder on it.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:147
#: fe8981e329ba465082c969e083579e02
msgid "**Connect the \"Safety Button\" to the Safety connector on the PX4IO board on the opposite side of the board from the Battery pads.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:151
#: b1cc89379866439b87f11865031ecbb5
msgid "Using a 3DR telemetry radio with your PX4FMU plus PX4IO system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:153
#: d13c2cf185fa4e3490c6e1394546d9ee
msgid "You will need a :ref:`3DR Radio <common-sik-telemetry-radio>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:154
#: 74030e5efb824b9985e33adaa471c3bf
msgid "Plug the telemetry adapter cable's large black connector into the 3DR radio as shown above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:156
#: 94b9d1591e2a448ea92e28008ca4a62d
msgid "The telemetry radio is shown above **incorrectly** connected to the FMU USART2 socket at the corner of the PX4IO board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:159
#: 9cde4897c464434c8666444147aa654a
msgid "**Correctly** plug the telemetry adapter cable's beige connector into the PX4IO boards **FMU UART5** socket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:161
#: a81595accc53451aad10753d44f17def
msgid "FMU UART5 is the middle socket on the end of the PX4IO board as indicated by the **red arrow** above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:163
#: b789679ee971470cb4ae0b2ad3524c5e
msgid "(FMU UARTx) means a port that is pass through connected directly from the PX4IO board to the PX4FMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:167
#: 0d52e1d63c904b99949275c176648ca5
msgid "Separate Servo power for high power applications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:172
#: e8b29ace6c33456ea792ff0a210e3684
msgid "**Using a separate power supply to provide power to the center servo power pins of the PX4IO board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:175
#: e507cec534c04e648bb71e188ae49b04
msgid "If you are driving high power servos with your PX4IO board you will want to provide servo power separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:177
#: 51a846c545fd4c77a5b78ba221bf07ad
msgid "In order to do this, remove the L1 Ferrite device circled in red on the image above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:179
#: d4a0cc437412438da1dbcb6bdf3a7513
msgid "Then run power from your separate power supply to one of the center pins of the Servo Connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:181
#: be8fda428bb346c1a5f0f8a7fa48ac28
msgid "And run the ground from your separate power supply to one of the servo connector pins nearest the edge of the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:185
#: 846aa1610a4344749d14f93ec913738c
msgid "Wiring your Motors and ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:187
#: a94273b6a1c3458e9c8b9fa835676d8a
msgid "Motor wiring and order for different frame shapes is covered in the topic :ref:`Connect ESCs and Motors <connect-escs-and-motors>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:191
#: 3e4deb9a0bb64165848c39427a18aa60
msgid "Using a Standard RC Radio Receiver with an 8 channel PPM Encoder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:193
#: cf3459157d184ddbb5f4cf223df4da5c
msgid "You can use a standard radio receiver with an 8 channel PPM Encoder in place of the PPM-SUM receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:196
#: 161c1c96b77041d1b6496c2be1837b5c
msgid "An 8 Channel PPM Encoder is `available from jDrones <http://store.jdrones.com/pixhawk_px4_paparazzi_ppm_encoder_v2_p/eleppmenc20.htm>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:198
#: 42f7d669a89d404d8874ccd5f497f566
msgid "Solder a 3x8 Right angle connector from the top into one end of the 8 Channel PPM Encoder board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:200
#: 3185fa1431704c4491ea95f0f95b9e3b
msgid "With the 3x8 connector up and facing away from you, solder a 3x1 Right angle connector on the right edge of the 8 Channel PPM Encoder board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:204
#: fabaec4032354af4b8a826d43ceb77e7
msgid "Connect 5-8 output channels of your receiver to the inputs of the 8 Channel Encoder (signal wire furthest from board) with 5-8 female to female servo jumpers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:208
#: dfc11fecf4c945fcb950a1657dedc557
msgid "Connect the PPM-SUM output of the Encoder with a 3 wire cable to the PX4IO boards PPM sum input (1x3 connector)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:213
#: 5a8caf3b2e0c4e55bd70fb0b667383fd
msgid "If you are using a 3DR PPM Encoder it is important to know that when you are calibrating your transmitter you will quite likely need to hook up your flight battery to the PX4IO because the USB port alone can't supply enough power."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:219
#: 614bdfc3988f4c5dac57ae58467d0e39
msgid "Compatible remote control (RC) receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:221
#: 2acbce988b8a4bb1aa9712b14bb9c368
msgid "PX4FMU is compatible with PPM remote control (RC) receivers, Futaba S.Bus receivers, and Spektrum DSM,DSM2, and DSM-X Satellite receivers. For traditional single-wire-per-channel (PWM) receivers a PPM encoder can be used to convert the receiver outputs to PPM-SUM.  Information about compatible receivers and how they are connected can be found in :ref:`this wiki page <common-rc-systems>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:230
#: c01b115943e64c7c884efe79f6212ef9
msgid "FRSky Taranis Transmitter"
msgstr ""
